xnu 0384: a GPU buffer of the calling process's pages (0x7d)

Turnip imports a texture over an IOSurface by the surface's base
address when its surface table does not name the id, and that path asked
the kernel for a buffer of those pages and got ENOSYS: the user client
knew 0x7e (a surface by id) and nothing beside it. Measured 2026-11-19,
the ring's line is "TU: error: import of host pages 0x... refused:
Function not implemented", and m2v_test's IOSurface texture reads
back zero because of it.

0x7d describes the range with IOMemoryDescriptor::withAddressRange()
on the calling task (which refuses an address the process does not own),
prepares it so the pages are wired, and hands it to the same
bufferAdopt() a surface takes: one IOVA, page by page. The descriptor is
completed when the buffer is freed.

